 the beat frequency of the resulting signal in <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"3.068ex\" height=\"1.57ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1356 694\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(888,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D467\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D467\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>? (Given that the speed of sound in air is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"9.051ex\" height=\"1.937ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -833.9 4000.7 855.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mspace\" transform=\"translate(1500,0)\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1667,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45A\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2545,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D460\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D460\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(502,363) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and the car reflects the sound at the frequency it has received). ","options":[],"correct_options":[],"explanation":"<p>It is given that the source emits sound of frequency f<sub>0</sub> = 492 Hz. The car is approaching the source and the speed of car is v = 2 m/s.</p>\n<p>Also, the speed of sound in air, v<sub>s</sub> = 330 m/s.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l0kkmhho/f66215e7-dd9c-48bf-af83-9f68d19b6510/f2d774c0-a035-11ec-9819-f5ef8e3b6498/file-1l0kkmhhp.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l0kkmhho/f66215e7-dd9c-48bf-af83-9f68d19b6510/f2d774c0-a035-11ec-9819-f5ef8e3b6498/file-1l0kkmhhp.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2017 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Waves Question 37 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l0kkmhho/f66215e7-dd9c-48bf-af83-9f68d19b6510/f2d774c0-a035-11ec-9819-f5ef8e3b6498/file-1l0kkmhhp.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l0kkmhho/f66215e7-dd9c-48bf-af83-9f68d19b6510/f2d774c0-a035-11ec-9819-f5ef8e3b6498/file-1l0kkmhhp.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l0kkmhho/f66215e7-dd9c-48bf-af83-9f68d19b6510/f2d774c0-a035-11ec-9819-f5ef8e3b6498/file-1l0kkmhhp.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l0kkmhho/f66215e7-dd9c-48bf-af83-9f68d19b6510/f2d774c0-a035-11ec-9819-f5ef8e3b6498/file-1l0kkmhhp.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l0kkmhho/f66215e7-dd9c-48bf-af83-9f68d19b6510/f2d774c0-a035-11ec-9819-f5ef8e3b6498/file-1l0kkmhhp.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l0kkmhho/f66215e7-dd9c-48bf-af83-9f68d19b6510/f2d774c0-a035-11ec-9819-f5ef8e3b6